title: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Retroactive authorization
route: /authorizations/new/:draftId?type=retro (Intake)
intro: A retroactive authorization asks for approval of care that was already given. Intake is the same onboarding form (imported, a known patient, or typed in) with the dates of service in the Request section, then why no authorization was in place and the supporting documents. Once a payer is chosen, one line quotes its Backdating rule, or says none is on file.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: every built-in payer has a Backdating rule. A payer added on Payers has none, which shows the 'No rule on file' wording.
---
start s1 "Pick 'Retroactive authorization' in 'Authorization type'\nOr open ?type=retro"
screen sc "Intake · Retroactive authorization\nThe row of ways in without 'Referrals', then the form, then one card for the reason and the documents"
goto gWays "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Start with a referral or patient"
goto gForm "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Patient, insurance and request rows"
decision dRule "Is a payer chosen, and has it a Backdating rule on file?"
process pNoLine "No line until a payer is chosen"
toast tRule "One line above the form\n'Summit's Backdating rule: ...'"
toast tNo "One amber line: 'No rule on file for Riverbend. Check with the payer.'\nReview & submit adds a note 'Retroactive rule'"
goto gPayers "Continues in: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Edit a rule"
screen sDup "'This looks like a request that already exists' only when one matches"
goto gDup "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Possible duplicate"
screen sReq "Request section: 'Level of care', 'First date of service', 'Last date of service'\nNo 'Request type': it is 'Retro-authorization'"
input iFrom "'First date of service' (required)"
input iTo "'Last date of service' (required)\nWithout it Review & submit asks the person to acknowledge it; the first date is what blocks"
decision dBad "Is the last date before the first?"
toast tBad "Field error: 'Before the first date'"
screen sWhy "'WHY IT WAS NOT OBTAINED AHEAD OF TIME'\nFour reasons to click, and 'Reason'"
click cChip "Click a reason\n'Coverage was pending when the patient was admitted', 'The patient was admitted after hours or on a weekend, and the notice window passed', 'The payer was not known on the day of admission', 'The notice was sent but the payer has no record of it'"
input iReason "Type or edit the 'Reason'"
decision dReason "Is the reason empty?"
toast tReason "Review & submit lists 'Why it was not obtained ahead of time' to acknowledge\n'The payer will ask why no authorization was in place. Add the reason.'"
screen sDoc "'SUPPORTING DOCUMENTS'\nDrop zone 'Admission order, eligibility check, attendance'"
input iDrop "Drop supporting documents, or click to choose files"
agent aRead "Reader sorts the files into the document list\nShown as chips with the file names"
store st "The request is recorded as 'Retro-authorization'\nDates of service, the reason and the files are kept on the case"
goto gElig "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Eligibility & Benefits › Retroactive authorization"
goto gDocs "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Clinical documentation › Required and typical documents by type"
click cSave "Click 'Save as draft'"
click cCont "Click 'Continue to Eligibility & Benefits'"
goto gSave "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Save as draft and leave"

s1 --> sc
sc -.-> gWays
sc -.-> gForm
sc --> dRule
dRule -->|No payer yet| pNoLine
dRule -->|Rule on file| tRule
dRule -->|No rule on file| tNo -.-> gPayers
sc --> sDup -.-> gDup
sc --> sReq --> iFrom --> iTo --> dBad
dBad -->|Yes| tBad --> iTo
dBad -->|No| sWhy
sWhy --> cChip --> iReason
sWhy --> iReason --> dReason
dReason -->|Yes| tReason --> sDoc
dReason -->|No| sDoc
sDoc --> iDrop --> aRead --> st
sDoc --> st
st --> gElig
st --> gDocs
st --> cSave --> gSave
st --> cCont --> gElig
